soundpost
=========

EARLST is a survival-aware model that reads the early-postoperative five-phase
Gd-EOB-DTPA MRI of the remnant liver and predicts the risk of hepatocellular
carcinoma recurrence over the first twenty-four months after curative-intent
resection. A three-dimensional state-space encoder reads the co-registered
phases; a small set of learnable queries distils the post-resection parenchyma
into an inspectable Remnant-State Token anchored to the hepatobiliary-phase
enhancement signal; a gated FiLM stage folds in the clinical-laboratory vector;
and a censoring-aware discrete-time head emits a calibrated recurrence-free
survival curve over twelve two-month intervals. Training uses the CRESCO
objective, which combines the censoring-aware likelihood with a differentiable
D-calibration term, a patient-pair ranking term and a hepatobiliary-phase
anchoring term so the probability scale is calibrated during training rather
than rescaled afterwards.

This package name borrows from instrument making: the soundpost is the small
dowel that carries an instrument's voice, the same role the Remnant-State Token
plays here.

Layout
------
  src/soundpost/tonewood    five-phase preprocessing, clinical encoding, cohorts
  src/soundpost/archings    encoders, Remnant-State Token, FiLM fusion, hazard head
  src/soundpost/voicing     CRESCO terms and the encoder pretext objectives
  src/soundpost/acoustics   discrimination, calibration and inference statistics
  src/soundpost/bench       optimiser, schedule, AMP, EMA, checkpointing, trainer
  src/soundpost/recital     prediction gathering and the metric report
  src/soundpost/jigs        seeding, logging, config loading
  src/soundpost/workshop    train / evaluate / infer / export entry points
  configs/                  composable model, data, train, optim, loss, eval groups

Installation
------------
pip:
    python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    pip install -e .

conda:
    conda env create -f environment.yml
    conda activate soundpost
    pip install -e .

docker:
    docker build -t soundpost .
    docker run --gpus all -it soundpost --help

The pinned stack is CUDA 11.7 with PyTorch 1.13.1 and Python 3.9; the selective
scan is written in plain PyTorch, so no custom CUDA kernels are required.

Data
----
The twenty-four-month curative-resection recurrence endpoint exists only in the
private EOB-RECUR cohort (3,200 patients, four sites, three vendors). It is
available upon reasonable request to the contributing institutions and cannot be
redistributed. The public liver datasets used for encoder pretraining and
external context, with their licences and verified access URLs, are listed in
sources.txt; run scripts/prepare_data.sh for a checklist. Each cohort manifest
is a JSON-lines file whose records point at the per-phase volume arrays, the
optional remnant-liver mask, the clinical fields, the time in months and the
event indicator.

A planted-signal synthetic cohort ships with the package (tonewood/synth.py) so
the full pipeline runs without any download; enable it with data.synthetic=true.

Training
--------
Primary result on the development sites:
    bash scripts/launch_train.sh configs/experiment/main.yaml data/eob_recur/train.jsonl

or directly:
    python -m soundpost.workshop train --config configs/experiment/main.yaml \
        --manifest data/eob_recur/train.jsonl --device cuda

Each reported ablation has its own experiment file:
    configs/experiment/ablation_no_rst.yaml          drop the Remnant-State Token
    configs/experiment/ablation_no_pretrain.yaml     skip VoCo + segmentation prior
    configs/experiment/ablation_swin_unetr.yaml      swap in the Swin backbone
    configs/experiment/ablation_resnet3d.yaml        swap in the 3D-ResNet backbone
    configs/experiment/ablation_likelihood_only.yaml CRESCO reduced to the likelihood
    configs/experiment/supplementary_selective.yaml  abstention / selective prediction
    configs/experiment/supplementary_recalibration.yaml  per-cohort intercept shift

Reported numbers are averaged over the ten seeds in configs/train/cresco.yaml.

Evaluation
----------
    python -m soundpost.workshop evaluate --config configs/experiment/main.yaml \
        --checkpoint runs/earlst/final.ckpt --manifest data/eob_recur/prospective.jsonl

Expected prospective primary cohort (Site D, n=1,080), mean over ten seeds:
    24-month AUROC          0.91  (95% CI 0.89-0.93; worst seed 0.898)
    Harrell concordance     0.81  (95% CI 0.78-0.83; worst seed 0.794)
    calibration slope       0.94      integrated calibration index 0.042
    net benefit @ 0.40      0.214     selective AUROC after 10% abstention 0.935
The likelihood-only ablation drops the slope to 0.78 and the D-calibration
p-value from 0.42 to 0.004; removing the Remnant-State Token drops AUROC to 0.88.

Export
------
    python -m soundpost.workshop export --config configs/experiment/main.yaml \
        --checkpoint runs/earlst/final.ckpt --output earlst_head.onnx
This traces the fusion-plus-hazard pathway given a Remnant-State vector and the
clinical embedding; the sequential state-space scan is kept in PyTorch.

Compute budget
--------------
The manuscript does not report a hardware profile. The defaults in
configs/experiment/main.yaml target 8x NVIDIA A100-80GB in fp32 at full
resolution: per-device micro-batch 2 with gradient accumulation 16 over 8 ranks
gives an effective batch of 256, AdamW at 2e-5 with 2,000 warmup steps and a
cosine decay over 800 epochs, EMA decay 0.9999. Full-resolution five-phase
128x128x128 volumes with the sequential scan make this storage- and
memory-heavy; budget several days of multi-GPU wall-clock and tens of gigabytes
of preprocessed volume cache.

Checkpoints
-----------
Checkpoints are written atomically and carry the optimiser state, the EMA shadow,
the resolved config and the random seed. Released weights are available upon
reasonable request.
